<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinando Carlo Gonzaga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1652–1708</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Charles IV, Duke of Mantua</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinando Carlo Gonzaga was the last Gonzaga Duke of Mantua and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a>, ruling from 1665. A pleasure-loving and extravagant prince, he sold Casale to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>. The emperor deposed him in 1708; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> annexed Mantua, Montferrat went to Savoy and France took Charleville.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinando-carlo-gonzaga.jpg" alt="Ferdinando Carlo Gonzaga" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hyacinthe Rigaud · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_painting_of_the_Duke_of_Mantua_(Ferdinando_Carlo_Gonzaga)_by_Hyacinthe_Rigaud.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
